IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- QUARANTINED FILE (BRIEF.md "Quarantine"; see TV-QUESTION.md): the Broadcasting Act 1994's First Schedule ("Broadcasting Apparatus") as a table of
-- versions on two time axes, and the kind of receiver it is asked about.  The Broadcasting Act folder owns the Broadcasting Act; this module takes
-- three of its deposited texts as plain facts and states what they say; nothing is imported from that folder.
--
-- THE VERSIONS (design: sgta-ta-versions.l4; assumed, not ruled).  Each is {effective day, published day}:
--   Revised Edition 2003 (31 Jul 2003): BA1994.20030731.txt:2134-2143 (items at 2139, 2141, 2143; definitions from 2146).  First Schedule items: 1 Broadcast television receiver;
--       2 Broadcast sound receiver; 3 Television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system).  Effective and published 31 Jul 2003 (the
--       edition's date).  The text does not show a Gazette day; the day is the edition's.
--   Revised Edition 2012 (31 Aug 2012): BA1994.20120831.txt:2163-2169 (items at 2167-2169; definitions 2171-2174).  The same three items.  Effective and published 31 Aug 2012.
--   G.N. No. S 549/2012: BA1994-S549-2012.txt.  Made 30 Oct 2012, "First published in the Government Gazette ... on 31st October 2012 at 5.00 pm",
--       and "shall be deemed to have come into operation on 1st January 2011".  It deletes the First Schedule and substitutes one with a single
--       item, the TVRO system.  Effective 1 Jan 2011, published 31 Oct 2012.
-- The Act's own history (BA1994.txt:4636-4650) lists S 549/2012 as the only notification amending the First Schedule; the current text
-- (BA1994.txt:4340-4357, version in force from 25/9/2024) lists the TVRO system alone.  Between the two Revised Editions the list is taken to be
-- unchanged because both print the same three items; that is an assumption about 2003 to 2012, not a text.  Before 31 Jul 2003 no text is deposited.
-- THE LICENSING REGULATIONS (a second Broadcasting Act input, deposited by the Broadcasting Act folder, read here for facts only): the Broadcasting (Television and Radio Licensing)
-- Regulations (Rg 1), Revised Edition 2004 (29 Feb 2004; broadcasting-television-and-radio-licensing-regulations/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-RG1.txt), provide the licences under
-- section 20(1) of the Act for broadcast sound receivers (Part IV, regs 23 to 26) and broadcast television receivers (Part V, regs 27 to 35), with fees in the First Schedule
-- (BA1994-RG1.txt:624-652); S 333/2004 (first published 15 Jun 2004, in operation 21 Jun 2004; BA1994-S333-2004.txt) amends them.  S 548/2012, the Broadcasting (Television and Radio
-- Licensing) (Revocation) Regulations 2012 (broadcasting-television-and-radio-licensing-revocation-regulations-2012/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S548-2012.txt), made 30 Oct 2012,
-- "First published in the Government Gazette ... on 31st October 2012 at 5.00 pm" (the same day and hour as S 549/2012), revokes Rg 1 (reg 2(1)) and "shall be deemed to have come into
-- operation on 1st January 2011" (reg 1); Rg 1 continues to apply to licences for periods before 1 Jan 2011 (reg 2(2)), and fees paid in advance for periods from 1 Jan 2011 are refunded in
-- full (reg 2(3)).  So Rg 1 is a version table too, with THREE rows (corrected 2026-11-04 on the team lead's reading of S 333/2004; before the correction this module had two rows and
-- said S 333/2004 "changes what Rg 1 says, not whether it is in operation, so it is not a row here", which hid what it changed):
--   Revised Edition 2004: effective and published 29 Feb 2004 (the edition's date; an earlier edition is not deposited).
--   S 333/2004: made 11 Jun 2004, first published 15 Jun 2004 at 5:00 pm, in operation 21 Jun 2004 (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:3, 21-23).  Among its 23 clauses: cl 2 deletes the definitions of "broadcast
--       sound receiver" and "broadcast television receiver" and defines "broadcasting apparatus", "commercial property" and "licence"; cl 3 deletes regs 3 and 4; cl 8 deletes regs 12 and 14;
--       cl 10 deletes regs 16 to 22 and substitutes a new reg 16; cl 11 substitutes reg 23(1) and (2); CL 12 SUBSTITUTES A PARAGRAPH FOR REG 27(1) AND (2), AND THE PARAGRAPH SAYS ONLY WHERE TO APPLY,
--       so reg 27(1)'s "No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence" stood only from 29 Feb 2004 to 20 Jun 2004; cl 14 inserts reg 29A; cl 19 replaces reg 36.
--   S 548/2012: effective 1 Jan 2011, published 31 Oct 2012 (the revocation).
-- What each version says in terms about a licence for a receiver, by kind and place, is a function below, with the line of the deposited text for each cell.
--
-- Which kind of receiver is which item: "broadcast sound receiver" means "any apparatus used for the aural reception of any broadcasting service"
-- (an FM or an AM broadcast radio); "broadcast television receiver" means "any apparatus used for the visual and aural reception in monochrome or
-- colour of any broadcasting service" (BA1994.20120831.txt:2171-2174).

DECLARE `Kind of receiver` IS ONE OF
    `television`
    `FM radio`
    `AM radio`
    `satellite dish system`

DECLARE `Is the receiver on the Broadcasting Act list` IS ONE OF
    `yes, the First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act 1994 lists it on that date`
    `no, the First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act 1994 does not list it on that date`
    `the First Schedule's list on that date is not known to this encoding`

-- The list in the two Revised Editions: items 1, 2 and 3.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of receiver`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`First Schedule, Revised Editions 2003 and 2012: the kind is listed` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `television` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `FM radio` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `AM radio` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `satellite dish system` THEN TRUE

-- The list substituted by S 549/2012: item 1, the TVRO system, alone.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of receiver`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012: the kind is listed` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `television` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `FM radio` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `AM radio` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `satellite dish system` THEN TRUE

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Is the receiver on the Broadcasting Act list`
`the list answer` MEANS
    IF b
    THEN `yes, the First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act 1994 lists it on that date`
    ELSE `no, the First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act 1994 does not list it on that date`

-- The latest-published version among those published on or before the reading day whose effective day is on or before the conduct day.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of receiver`
      `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Is the receiver on the Broadcasting Act list`
`the First Schedule lists the kind of receiver, for the conduct day as read on the reading day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 31 10 2012)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011)) THEN `the list answer` (`First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012: the kind is listed` k)
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 31 8 2012)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 31 8 2012)) THEN `the list answer` (`First Schedule, Revised Editions 2003 and 2012: the kind is listed` k)
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 31 7 2003)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 31 7 2003)) THEN `the list answer` (`First Schedule, Revised Editions 2003 and 2012: the kind is listed` k)
           OTHERWISE `the First Schedule's list on that date is not known to this encoding`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The licensing regulations (Rg 1): three versions on the two axes.  The latest-published version among those published on or before the reading day whose effective day is on or
-- before the conduct day; NOTHING before 29 Feb 2004 (no earlier edition is deposited).

DECLARE `Rg 1 version` IS ONE OF
    `Rg 1, Revised Edition 2004`
    `Rg 1 as amended by S 333/2004`
    `Rg 1 as revoked by S 548/2012`

GIVEN `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Rg 1 version`
`Rg 1: the version for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 31 10 2012)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011)) THEN JUST `Rg 1 as revoked by S 548/2012`  -- S 548/2012, published 31 Oct 2012, deemed in operation 1 Jan 2011
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 15 6 2004)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 21 6 2004)) THEN JUST `Rg 1 as amended by S 333/2004`  -- first published 15 Jun 2004, in operation 21 Jun 2004
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 29 2 2004)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 29 2 2004)) THEN JUST `Rg 1, Revised Edition 2004`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Is Rg 1 in operation?  JUST TRUE for the Revised Edition 2004 and for it as amended by S 333/2004; JUST FALSE once S 548/2012 has revoked it for the conduct day (and the reader has it);
-- NOTHING where no edition is deposited.  This says whether the regulations existed, NOT what they required: that is the next function.
GIVEN `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 1, the television and radio licensing regulations, are in operation for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Rg 1: the version for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` `conduct day` `reading day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN
        CONSIDER v
        WHEN `Rg 1, Revised Edition 2004` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `Rg 1 as amended by S 333/2004` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `Rg 1 as revoked by S 548/2012` THEN JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Place of the receiver` IS ONE OF
    `in a house or flat`
    `in a vehicle`
    `in a vessel that has no ship station licence`
    `in a commercial property`

-- What a version of Rg 1 says IN TERMS about a licence for a kind of receiver in a place.  A string of the regulation and its words, taken from the deposited texts (BA1994-RG1.txt is
-- the Revised Edition 2004; BA1994-S333-2004.txt the amending regulations), or a statement that no regulation of the version says so in terms.  The Broadcasting Act's s 20(1) is not a
-- regulation and is not in this table.  "Commercial property" is defined only from S 333/2004 (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:34-42): premises permitted to be used wholly or partly for business, or
-- occupied by a charity, other than a hotel, hospital or institution providing education or instruction.
GIVEN v IS A `Rg 1 version`
      k IS A `Kind of receiver`
      p IS A `Place of the receiver`
GIVETH A STRING
`what Rg 1 in the version says in terms about a licence for the kind of receiver in the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `Rg 1, Revised Edition 2004` THEN
        BRANCH IF k EQUALS `satellite dish system` THEN "Rg 1, Revised Edition 2004, reg 2(1): the definition of 'broadcast television receiver' ends 'but does not include any Television Receive-Only Satellite Receiving System' (BA1994-RG1.txt:144-148), so a TVRO system is outside the 'broadcast television receiver' of reg 27(1)"
               IF k EQUALS `television` AND (p EQUALS `in a vehicle` OR p EQUALS `in a vessel that has no ship station licence`) THEN "reg 27(1): 'No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence' (BA1994-RG1.txt:481-482); and reg 28(2): 'A separate licence shall be required for every broadcast television receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:501-504)"
               IF k EQUALS `television` THEN "reg 27(1): 'No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence' (BA1994-RG1.txt:481-482)"
               IF p EQUALS `in a vehicle` OR p EQUALS `in a vessel that has no ship station licence` THEN "reg 23(1): 'A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:441-444)"
               OTHERWISE "no regulation of the Revised Edition 2004 says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver there; reg 27(3) says a television licence 'shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers' at the address (BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), and item 2 of the First Schedule prices 'Licence for a broadcast sound receiver' at $27 for 12 months (BA1994-RG1.txt:629)"
    WHEN `Rg 1 as amended by S 333/2004` THEN
        BRANCH IF k EQUALS `satellite dish system` THEN "S 333/2004 cl 2 deletes the definitions of 'broadcast television receiver' (and with it the words that excluded a TVRO system) and of 'TVRO system' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:29-31, 48-52), and cl 10 deletes reg 16 'Broadcasting system not to include TVRO system'; the amended text does not say in terms whether a dish system is within it"
               IF k EQUALS `television` AND p EQUALS `in a commercial property` THEN "reg 29A(1), inserted by S 333/2004 cl 14: 'A separate licence shall be required for every broadcast television receiver installed in a commercial property' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:162-167)"
               IF k EQUALS `television` AND (p EQUALS `in a vehicle` OR p EQUALS `in a vessel that has no ship station licence`) THEN "reg 28(2), which S 333/2004 does not amend (cl 13 amends reg 28(1) and (5)): 'A separate licence shall be required for every broadcast television receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:501-504; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:149-160)"
               IF k EQUALS `television` THEN "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required to operate a broadcast television receiver in a house or flat: S 333/2004 cl 12(a) deletes reg 27(1) and (2) and substitutes a paragraph (1) that says only 'An application for a licence to install or operate a broadcast television receiver may be made at any post office or at such other places as the Authority may require' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:137-144); reg 27(3) remains ('A licence shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers by the licensee, members of his family and domestic servants resident at the address specified therein', BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), reg 27(4), amended by cl 12(b) to say 'installed or operated by', requires a separate licence for a television installed or operated by a lodger, boarder, resident guest or any person occupying a portion of the premises under a separate tenancy (BA1994-RG1.txt:489-493; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:145-146), and reg 7 now speaks of a contravention of 'section 20 (1) of the Act' alone, cl 6 having deleted 'or of regulation 17, 27 or 36' (BA1994-RG1.txt:264-266; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:92-94)"
               IF p EQUALS `in a vessel that has no ship station licence` THEN "reg 23(2), substituted by S 333/2004 cl 11: 'A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:123-133)"
               IF p EQUALS `in a vehicle` THEN "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver in a vehicle: S 333/2004 cl 11(a) deletes reg 23(1) and (2) and substitutes a paragraph (1) on where to apply and a paragraph (2) that names a vessel only (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:123-133)"
               IF p EQUALS `in a commercial property` THEN "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver there; reg 29A(2), inserted by S 333/2004, says a licence under reg 29A(1) 'shall permit the use of one or more broadcast sound receivers' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:168-169)"
               OTHERWISE "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver there; reg 27(3) says a television licence 'shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers' at the address (BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), and item 2 of the First Schedule, which S 333/2004 does not amend, prices 'Licence for a broadcast sound receiver' at $27 for 12 months (BA1994-RG1.txt:629)"
    WHEN `Rg 1 as revoked by S 548/2012` THEN "S 548/2012 reg 2(1) revokes Rg 1, deemed in operation on 1 January 2011, first published 31 October 2012; reg 2(2) keeps Rg 1 for licences granted under s 20(1) of the Act for periods before 1 January 2011 (BA1994-S548-2012.txt:28-57): the revoked regulations say nothing about the conduct"

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of receiver`
      p IS A `Place of the receiver`
      `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A STRING
`what Rg 1 says in terms about a licence for the kind of receiver in the place, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Rg 1: the version for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` `conduct day` `reading day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "no edition of Rg 1 is deposited for that conduct day as read on that reading day (the earliest deposited text is the Revised Edition 2004, in operation from 29 February 2004)"
    WHEN JUST v THEN `what Rg 1 in the version says in terms about a licence for the kind of receiver in the place` v k p

-- The two Broadcasting Act instruments move together: for a television or a sound receiver, Rg 1 is in operation exactly when the First Schedule lists the receiver.  NOTHING for a
-- satellite dish system (Rg 1's licences are for broadcast sound and television receivers; the TVRO system has its own regulations, which are not modelled here) and wherever either is not known.
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rg 1 in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two agree` MEANS `Rg 1 in operation` EQUALS b

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of receiver`
      `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 is in operation exactly when the First Schedule lists the receiver, for the conduct day as read on the reading day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF k EQUALS `satellite dish system` THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `Rg 1, the television and radio licensing regulations, are in operation for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` `conduct day` `reading day`
               WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
               WHEN JUST r THEN
                   CONSIDER `the First Schedule lists the kind of receiver, for the conduct day as read on the reading day` k `conduct day` `reading day`
                   WHEN `yes, the First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act 1994 lists it on that date` THEN JUST (`the two agree` TRUE r)
                   WHEN `no, the First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act 1994 does not list it on that date` THEN JUST (`the two agree` FALSE r)
                   WHEN `the First Schedule's list on that date is not known to this encoding` THEN NOTHING
